+## Explicit native runtime composition (V10)
+
+Only an explicit daemon invocation may construct the native factory. It requires
+selected compositor signature, PID/start and Wayland display matching the current
+process environment, both compositor IPC and Wayland sockets owned by this UID,
+and connected peers with that exact compositor PID/start. No lookup selects
+another session or falls back to a physical compositor. Startup strips all
+request-scoped HYPR_WINDOWCTL_* flags. Each core native operation restores only
+the explicit per-member family-single/preview-ready flags and exact captured ID/PID.
+
+Executable source material must match the explicitly expected SHA256 on an open
+file descriptor with stable stat before use. Those exact bytes are copied into
+an executable sealed memfd (WRITE/GROW/SHRINK/SEAL), so both path replacement and
+in-place edits after proof cannot change execution. Producer launch executes that
+sealed FD. Core commit likewise hashes, seals and executes the exact core FD with its explicit
+ID/PID arguments. Every actor owns an independent desktop/capture root and one
+renderer transport. The failure sink is bound only after controller construction;
+an early transport failure is retained and delivered once after binding instead
+of being lost or addressing a previous actor.
+
+The API client never starts a daemon or retries an uncertain accepted request
+through a native fallback. It verifies the runtime owner, session, socket inode,
+SO_PEERCRED PID/start before sending. No response is truthful failure with unknown
+acceptance; completion remains separate from accepted receipt. Native recovery
+and automatic production frontend replacement are not included in this stage.
